    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d475">

                <pb facs="0423" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.8591/942</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Veracruz</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cochran</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 119</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Veracruz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-04-23">April 23, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        25.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to despatch no.
                    97 from this office, dated April 2, 1940,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d475-f1"/>
                    reporting that the German tanker <hi rendition="#italic">Tine Asmussen</hi>, <pb
                        facs="0424" n="412" xml:id="pg412"/> which had been anchored for some time
                    in the bay of Coatzacoalcos, had been bought by Mexico.</p>
                <p>The local daily newspaper, <hi rendition="#italic">El Dictamen</hi>, today
                    carries a short news item from Coatzacoalcos, dated April 22, reporting that the
                    Mexican flag was raised on the vessel at 3 o’clock that day and that it had been
                    given the name of <hi rendition="#italic">Juan Casiano</hi>. It is reported that
                    the new Mexican tanker is the largest of the ships belonging to Petroleos
                    Mexicanos. It is believed that the implications of this transfer of the title of
                    a German ship are well known to the Department.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> P. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Cochran, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
